==English==
{{wikipedia|lang=en}}
[[Image:Bell 206L3 (D-HASA).jpg|thumb|right|A '''helicopter''' (aircraft).]]
[[File:Acer circinatum 9468.JPG|thumb|a [[samara]] or '''helicopter''']]

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*welH-|*peth₂-}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|hélicoptère}}, from {{uder|en|grc|-}} {{af|grc|ἕλιξ|t1=spiral|πτερόν|t2=wing|nocat=1}}. {{doublet|en|helicopteron}}. {{surf|en|helico-|-pter}}. The dragonfly sense is from a dragonfly's ability to hover and fly in any direction, like the flying machine.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|AusE}} {{IPA|en|/ˈheliˌkɔptə(ɹ)/}}
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈhɛl.iˌkɒp.tə(ɹ)/|/ˈhɛl.ɪˌkɒp.tə(ɹ)/}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈhɛlɪˌkɑptɚ/}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-helicopter.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|aviation}} An [[aircraft]] that is borne along by one or more sets of long rotating [[blade]]s which allow it to hover, move in any [[direction]] including [[reverse]], or land; and typically having a smaller set of blades on its tail to stabilize the [[aircraft]].
#: {{hyper|en|aircraft}} 
#: {{ux|en|We flew over the city in a '''helicopter'''.}}
# A powered [[trowel]]ing machine with spinning blades used to spread [[concrete]].
# {{lb|en|botany}} The winged fruit of certain trees, such as [[ash]], [[elm]], and [[maple]].
# {{lb|en|zoology|slang}} A [[dragonfly]]; so named due to its resemblance to a helicopter (sense 1).
# A whirling trick performed with [[devil sticks]].
# A [[breakdance]] move in which the dancer [[spin]]s on the floor while extending the legs to [[resemble]] the [[blade]]s of a helicopter.

